<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bakwena</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as BaKwena</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bakwena are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tswana-people">Tswana people</a> who trace their origin to a split from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahurutshe">Bahurutshe</a> and who in turn gave rise to the Bangwato and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangwaketse">Bangwaketse</a>. Settled in what is now south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/botswana">Botswana</a>, they were rebuilt in the 19th century by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sechele-i">Sechele I</a>, who made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/molepolole">Molepolole</a> their capital. Their territory became part of the Bechuanaland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> in 1885 and is now Botswana's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kweneng-district">Kweneng District</a>.</p></div>
